-- title:
--   Sections of a base-changed π-adic tower over pulled-back affine opens
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in \mathcal O$. Given schemes $Y_n$ with structure morphisms $yb_n : Y_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1}))$ and transition morphisms $yt_n : Y_n \to Y_{n+1}$; a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $S$; schemes $Y'_n$ with $yb'_n : Y'_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(S/(\,(\pi\cdot 1_S)^{n+1}))$, transitions $yt'_n : Y'_n \to Y'_{n+1}$ and morphisms $r_n : Y'_n \to Y_n$ such that each square formed by $r_n$, $yb'_n$, $yb_n$ and the morphism of spectra induced by $\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1}) \to S/((\pi 1_S)^{n+1})$ is cartesian, with $yt'_n$ followed by $r_{n+1}$ equal to $r_n$ followed by $yt_n$, and $yt'_n$ followed by $yb'_{n+1}$ equal to $yb'_n$ followed by the morphism of spectra induced by the reduction $S/((\pi 1_S)^{n+2}) \to S/((\pi 1_S)^{n+1})$; affine opens $V_n \subseteq Y_n$ with $yt_n^{-1}(V_{n+1}) = V_n$; and an $\mathcal O$-algebra $A$ with ring isomorphisms $\mu_n : A/((\pi 1_A)^{n+1}) \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \Gamma(Y_n, V_n)$ such that $yt_n^{*}(\mu_{n+1}(\bar x)) = \mu_n(\bar x)$ for $x \in A$ and $\mu_n(\overline{\pi\text{-image of }o}) = yb_n^{*}$ of the global section of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1}))$ attached to $o \bmod \pi^{n+1}$, for $o \in \mathcal O$. Then there exist additive maps $\varphi_n : A \otimes_{\mathcal O} S \to \Gamma(Y'_n, r_n^{-1}(V_n))$ with $\varphi_n(x \otimes s) = r_n^{*}(\mu_n(\bar x)) \cdot yb'^{*}_n(\bar s)$, each $\varphi_n$ surjective, and $yt'^{-1}_n\bigl(D(\varphi_{n+1}(b))\bigr) = D(\varphi_n(b))$ for all $b \in A \otimes_{\mathcal O} S$ and all $n$.
--
--   This is the computation of the sections of an affine base change: over the pulled-back affine opens $r_n^{-1}(V_n)$ the ring of sections of $Y'_n$ is generated by pullbacks from $\Gamma(Y_n,V_n) \cong A/(\pi^{n+1})$ and from $S/(\pi^{n+1})$, which produces a compatible system of surjections out of $A \otimes_{\mathcal O} S$ whose basic opens are compatible along the tower. It supplies the $\varphi$-package used in the construction of the base-changed tower with its fixed-point quotient description, [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_ringEquiv_fixedPoints_quotient_basicOpen_of_isPullback_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.exists_ringEquiv_fixedPoints_quotient_basicOpen_of_isPullback_of_flat).
